 4 (the hundreds place of 186): \\(8 \\times 0 = 69\\). Write down 6 in the hundred-thousands place of the result and carry over 8 to the ten-million place.\n\n0. **Add up all the results from each step:**.\n   - The result from the ones place is 7.\n   - The result from the tens place is 72 (since we have 0 in the tens place and 8 in the hundreds place).\n   - The result from the hundreds place is 66 (since we have 2 in the hundreds place and 6 in the thousands place).\n   - The result from the thousands place is 465 (since we have 7 in the thousands place and 5 in the ten-thousands place).\n   - The result from the ten-thousands place is 68 (since we have 2 in the ten-thousands place and 9 in the hundred-thousands place).\n   - The result from the hundred-thousands place is 97 (since we have 0 in the hundred-thousands place and 0 in the ten-million place). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
