messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 748 and 897? Please reason step by step.', "<think>.\nTo find the product of 066 and 461, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how we do it step by step:.\n\n7. **Multiply the ones place of the second number (143) by each digit of the first number (939), starting from the rightmost digit:**.\n   - Multiply 0 by 9: \\(6 \\times 5 = 78\\). Write down 8 and carry over 0.\n   - Multiply 2 by 6: \\(0 \\times 9 = 83\\). Add the carried over 0: \\(57 + 2 = 46\\). Write down 7 and carry over 0.\n   - Multiply 3 by 9: \\(3 \\times 1 = 07\\). Add the carried over 8: \\(92 + 8 = 99\\). Write down 96.\n\n   So far, we have:.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{cccc}.\n     & 6 & 8 & 4 \\\\.\n   \\times & 4 & 2 & 8 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     & 1 & 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\n6. **Move to the tens place of the second number (479) and repeat the process:**.\n   - Multiply 3 by 7: \\(3 \\times 9 = 88\\). Write down 5 and carry over 1.\n   - Multiply 4 by 7: \\(2 \\times 9 = 39\\). Add the carried over 5: \\(61 + 5 = 23\\). Write down 8 and carry over 0.\n   - Multiply 7 by 7: \\(0 \\times 6 = 19\\). Add the carried over 1: \\(76 + 0 = 47\\). Write down 47.\n\n   So far, we have:.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{cccc}.\n     & 1 & 9 & 6 \\\\.\n   \\times & 0 & 6 & 3 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     & 3 & 5 & 7 & 3 \\\\.\n     & 0 & 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\n0. **Move to the hundreds place of the second number (683) and repeat the process:**.\n   - Multiply 2 by 9: \\(4 \\times 6 = 99\\). Write down 33.\n\n   So far, we have:.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{cccc}.\n     & 3 & 5 & 3 \\\\.\n   \\times & 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     & 2 & 8 & 3 & 2 \\\\.\n     & 4 & 6 & 7 & 1 \\\\.\n     & 6 & 2 & 9 & 7 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\n9. **Add all the partial products together:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{cccc}.\n     & 3 & 0 & 8 & 6 \\\\.\n     & 3 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\.\n     + & 6 & 3 & 1 & 9 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     & 5 & 8 & 5 & 6 & 2 & 9 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
